+### Switching the rendering GPU at runtime
+
+`setrendergpu` makes another DRM device the primary (rendering) GPU and
+rebuilds the renderer on it. It needs a wlroots with dynamic primary GPU
+support (`WLR_DRM_HAS_DYNAMIC_PRIMARY`); otherwise it only logs an error.
+`recreate` rebuilds the renderer on the current GPU and works with any wlroots.
+
+```sh
+mmsg dispatch setrendergpu,card1             # card or render node name
+mmsg dispatch setrendergpu,/dev/dri/renderD128
+mmsg dispatch setrendergpu,recreate
+```
+
+With `WLR_DRM_DYNAMIC_PRIMARY=1` in the environment, wlroots does this on its
+own when outputs are hot-plugged (e.g. a display mux moving the internal panel
+to the other GPU). `MANGO_LOG_LEVEL=info` (or `debug`) makes wlroots log those
+switches without the full output of `-d`.
+
